WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.832
(cheering and applause)

00:00:04.832 --> 00:00:07.016
(cheering and applause)

00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:08.306
That's nice,

00:00:08.306 --> 00:00:11.346
(cheering and applause)

00:00:11.346 --> 00:00:13.350
It never gets old. Does it?

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.183
Never does.

00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:15.510
(laughter)

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.310
You should at least pretend
it gets old sometimes.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.441
It doesn't get old.
Doesn't get old?

00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:19.274
I'm not gonna pretend

00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:21.154
You walk into a pizza parlor
and everybody does that

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.151
They all stand up,

00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:23.160
(laughter)

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.950
I've never eaten a pizza in me life.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:25.830
You've never had a pizza?

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.663
Never had a pizza
We gotta get you a pizza

00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:28.120
Big news!

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.520
Would you stop making noise over there,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.680
He just hit his tambourine.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.702
Anyway, good rocking, that was great

00:00:32.702 --> 00:00:34.003
They did a good job. Didn't they?

00:00:34.003 --> 00:00:36.350
A great band you're lucky.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.260
Well, I think they're lucky
Well you would

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.277
To work with a man of
my talent and ability.

00:00:41.277 --> 00:00:43.303
Okay. That was embarrassing.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.568
First of all, I, we've talked before,

00:00:46.568 --> 00:00:49.810
you know that I'm one of those
people that knows more about

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.850
you than you know about you.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:52.683
I do.

00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:55.400
Yeah. It's, I'm one of
those people that has the,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.738
the books, and the bootlegs,
and the rare bootleg

00:00:58.738 --> 00:01:01.374
unreleased of you guys
tuning your instruments,

00:01:01.374 --> 00:01:03.881
and sleeping and making chili.

00:01:03.881 --> 00:01:05.070
(laughter)

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.706
And you must, it must
be kind of weird to meet

00:01:07.706 --> 00:01:10.130
people like me because it's like,

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.746
you've just lived your life
and you did these great things,

00:01:12.746 --> 00:01:14.143
but it's just your life.

00:01:14.143 --> 00:01:16.767
Yes, but I have to rely
on people like you now.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:17.600
Why is that?

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.581
I have no memory.

00:01:18.581 --> 00:01:21.710
You forgot everything.
Tell me everything

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.660
So I can tell you that On March 5th, 1968,

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.310
I was with you yes,
You had an amazing bagel

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:30.202
Yeah, no, there, there really
hasn't been, for example,

00:01:30.202 --> 00:01:32.931
there were these, I think
there's one, isn't it this week,

00:01:32.931 --> 00:01:33.859
Frank, that there's,

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:37.420
there's one of these Beatles
conventions where all the

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.740
people come together and
it borders on craziness.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.573
I haven't gone to those,

00:01:41.573 --> 00:01:44.780
but it borders on craziness
where they have soap

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.540
that's of your head, and
they're praying to it. I mean,

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.880
Let me tell you, I've
never been to one either.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.270
You've never gone to a Beatles convention?

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.630
No but a lot of people who do go say

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:53.670
they have a good time.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.503
Oh that's good.

00:01:54.503 --> 00:01:56.333
The only problem I have with it,

00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:58.245
that a lot of the stuff they're selling,

00:01:58.245 --> 00:02:01.907
is sort of stuff from
now, and not from then

00:02:01.907 --> 00:02:03.583
Its not like the old stuff, right

00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:05.327
It's like they make a guitar and,

00:02:05.327 --> 00:02:06.310
They do

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:08.487
Right, or they say this
is an actual, you know.

00:02:08.487 --> 00:02:11.400
And they make my head out of soap.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.233
(laughter)

00:02:12.233 --> 00:02:13.998
Actually, I did that.

00:02:13.998 --> 00:02:18.991
I'm curious. You have been
super, super famous now for,

00:02:18.991 --> 00:02:21.773
for over 40 years,

00:02:21.773 --> 00:02:23.195
Yup

00:02:23.195 --> 00:02:24.028
You know, I think about

00:02:24.028 --> 00:02:26.956
I've been famous longer than
you've been on this planet.

00:02:26.956 --> 00:02:29.750
It's true. That's
actually a true statement.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.170
Cause you're 35 now. Right?

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.400
I'm 28, actually, but you're very close

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.020
and I'm getting, next year
I'll be, I'll be 25, next year.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.169
Nah, you're going down.
Looking forward to that,

00:02:40.169 --> 00:02:41.297
No, I, you,

00:02:41.297 --> 00:02:42.950
And you think about
it, I was thinking you,

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.360
can you even remember when
you weren't Ringo Starr,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.530
when you were just Richard Starkey,

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.480
normal guy walking around,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.513
do you remember being Richard
Starkey, a normal fella?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.350
(laughter)

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.183
I'm thinking,

00:02:56.183 --> 00:02:57.981
You're thinking? You always
nod your head like that

00:02:57.981 --> 00:02:59.510
when you think?
yeah I do when I'm thinking

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.550
Cause that's a real problem.
I know

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.950
Hey don't point out my problems.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.080
Okay. Lets talk about my problems

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.230
Anyway. Yeah, that was a long time ago.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:10.030
And I lost my family. You
know, my children don't say,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.730
Hey Ringo, do you want a cup of tea?

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:12.563
Right?

00:03:12.563 --> 00:03:14.693
They say, hi, dad and darling.

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:17.260
I called you darling earlier
and you didn't like it.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.389
I wasn't going to mention it

00:03:19.389 --> 00:03:20.222
(laughter)

00:03:20.222 --> 00:03:21.488
That's very nice of you.

00:03:21.488 --> 00:03:23.710
You're, you once said to your mother,

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.880
I read this in an interview,
you once said to your mother,

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.530
all people over the age
of 60 should be shot.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.519
Yes. I used to think as a teenager,

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:33.250
anyone at 60 should be shot.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.610
They were just taking
up space on the planet.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.613
Right, So I'm just curious.
How old are you now?

00:03:38.613 --> 00:03:40.092
Time to be shot.

00:03:40.092 --> 00:03:45.092
(laughter and applause)

00:03:45.126 --> 00:03:47.370
Lets not have that,
Lets not have that,

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.229
But anyway, the other line,
My mother, when I was 40,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:54.237
my mother who remembered
everything, as mothers do.

00:03:54.237 --> 00:03:58.770
Said when I was 40, happy
birthday son, I don't suppose

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.190
you still think like you
used to, about 60 year olds.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.863
And I said, no, not anymore, mom.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.268
It was funny at the time.

00:04:06.268 --> 00:04:10.438
(laughter)

00:04:10.438 --> 00:04:11.750
How do we have proof!
Have to be there

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.953
We could look it up in a book

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.046
What do you think of, these days

00:04:16.046 --> 00:04:21.046
there's this phenomenon
where pop stars don't come up

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.730
the way the Beatles came up where it was

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.680
a very organic experience,
there are pop groups that

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.990
are put together and
they're sort of packaged.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.316
There are shows like
American idol, which began

00:04:32.316 --> 00:04:35.580
in England and has come over
here and become a big success.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.074
Are you comfortable with that phenomenon?

00:04:37.074 --> 00:04:39.228
I don't take much of an interest in it.

00:04:39.228 --> 00:04:41.591
I mean, I come from, as
you said, I come from,

00:04:41.591 --> 00:04:43.476
first of all, get your instrument,

00:04:43.476 --> 00:04:46.510
then playing with
friends, playing in clubs,

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.410
playing in theaters, playing,
in our case, stadiums.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.243
Right,

00:04:50.243 --> 00:04:54.130
Well, you know, I play
for the joy of playing.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:56.968
My dream was to play drums, which I do

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:59.299
and to play with good players,

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.690
and then play with great
players, which I still am.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.530
So, you know, my dreams
are still coming to,

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.915
and I'm still playing. So that's good.

00:05:06.915 --> 00:05:10.040
The ones they put together,
I don't understand it

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.872
really because you put like
five strangers in a room,

00:05:12.872 --> 00:05:16.910
you tell them what to
sing, some producer will

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.712
take a line from that
one, a line from this one,

00:05:18.712 --> 00:05:21.730
they'll go on stage
pretending they had something

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:22.780
to do with this,

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:23.613
Right,

00:05:23.613 --> 00:05:24.900
And then the minute it's not working,

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.150
they just get dumped.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.370
Right,

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.610
They also do a strange thing,

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.910
which is they tell people
what their personality is.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:31.743
Yeah.

00:05:31.743 --> 00:05:34.453
You're the tough one, you're
the cuddly one, whereas

00:05:34.453 --> 00:05:36.118
Conan's the tall one,

00:05:36.118 --> 00:05:40.048
I was going to go for sexy,
but you went for tall,

00:05:40.048 --> 00:05:40.881
(laughter)

00:05:40.881 --> 00:05:41.920
Tall and sexy,

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.236
Thank you. That'll be,

00:05:43.236 --> 00:05:46.880
I like it when you say it.
Sexy

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:51.118
Yeah, people just tuning
in, Oh, there we are, Hi!

00:05:51.118 --> 00:05:53.400
(laughter)

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.740
But its funny because one
of the things that was

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.830
so great about the experience
you went through was

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.840
that it was all organic and real.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.630
Everyone had their own identity
and that came through and

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.020
today I think they would
be saying, 'Okay, John,

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.750
we're going to make you
this one, and we're going

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.590
to make Paul this one,
and Ringo that one,'

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.157
And it seems like a very odd way,

00:06:12.157 --> 00:06:14.898
If they ever do that I'd
like them to make me taller,

00:06:14.898 --> 00:06:16.910
(laughter)

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.060
I have a lot of pull with these people,

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.620
Ill see what I can do.
I know I can tell,

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.098
Don't be sarcastic, now,

00:06:21.098 --> 00:06:22.474
(laughter)

00:06:22.474 --> 00:06:25.050
now you're playing a song tonight for us,

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.780
which is called never without you.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:27.613
Yes.

00:06:27.613 --> 00:06:28.870
This is a tribute to George Harrison.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.703
Exactly.

00:06:29.703 --> 00:06:32.710
And first of all, my condolences that,

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.950
that this season is necessary to do,

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.790
Well, you know, the song, you know,

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:42.100
George has gone physically,
but spiritually,

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.031
he's still with us through
his friendship with me,

00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:50.170
and his music. So the song is about that,

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:52.893
He's still, he's still with us anyway.

00:06:52.893 --> 00:06:55.610
Right. Right. And this is a,

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:58.390
that's gotta be a powerful
thing to perform for people.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.440
It is, I mean, You know,

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.250
though we've been on this role now

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.133
promoting the record Ringo Rama,

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:06.390
and mainly playing this song,

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:10.944
It's still an emotional moment,
especially when I've put in,

00:07:10.944 --> 00:07:15.036
in the song words that George has written.

00:07:15.036 --> 00:07:17.263
You know, from never with,

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.734
I'm having a moment.

00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:24.213
You don't even know who I am right now.

00:07:25.838 --> 00:07:27.300
Yes I do. Yes I do Ted Koppel

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.360
It's coming back, its coming
back, within you without.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.193
Right

00:07:32.193 --> 00:07:34.140
Some of his lines have
been put in the song.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:35.924
So all things must pass,

00:07:35.924 --> 00:07:36.757
Right.

00:07:36.757 --> 00:07:39.200
So, you know, it was, for me,

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:41.553
it was a nice way to
say, you know, I know,

00:07:41.553 --> 00:07:44.086
I knew George loved me. I loved George.

00:07:44.086 --> 00:07:45.957
And this is a song for him.

00:07:45.957 --> 00:07:50.190
What's also nice is that you got Clapton,

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.147
is to play on it.

00:07:51.147 --> 00:07:54.220
It was the only guitarist
I would have on this track

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:57.211
because they, George and
Eric, had a great relationship

00:07:57.211 --> 00:07:58.910
and Eric and I, and George knows,

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.850
So I wanted him to play on the
record and we called him up

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:02.890
and he said, okay.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.490
What was nice is there, was
this amazing tribute at the,

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.120
was it the Royal Albert Hall?
Royal Albert Hall

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.690
for George, And I think this
is just a few months ago.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.320
It was last November, the 29th.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.100
Yeah. And it was, I, I
didn't, wasn't able to go,

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.880
but everyone told me that it
had the spirit of a party,

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.570
which was probably what he
would have wanted something and

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.580
all these great musicians
who knew and loved him coming

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.730
together and playing his music.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.970
That's the point, everybody
on stage knew George,

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:30.030
He knew them. It wasn't
like, we're doing a charity,

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.380
let's call Conan, You know.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.174
(laughter)

00:08:34.174 --> 00:08:36.539
I waited by the phone Ringo.

00:08:36.539 --> 00:08:37.403
Yeah. But you know,

00:08:37.403 --> 00:08:39.684
I sat by that phone for hours waiting,

00:08:39.684 --> 00:08:42.380
call never came. I play a mean Moraccas,

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.213
But you know what I mean?

00:08:43.213 --> 00:08:45.360
It was all the people that
loved him, He loved them,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.379
He knew them, So it was great
that we all played together.

00:08:48.379 --> 00:08:49.212
Right.

00:08:49.212 --> 00:08:50.930
And then we all hung
out together was great.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.720
We all had our George
stories, and our moments.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:54.553
Sure.

00:08:54.553 --> 00:08:55.635
It was really a cool thing to do.

00:08:55.635 --> 00:08:58.280
Well, we're thrilled that you're here,

00:08:58.280 --> 00:08:59.643
We're also thrilled that you're gonna play

00:08:59.643 --> 00:09:00.632
this song for you.

00:09:00.632 --> 00:09:02.930
It's just, it's a real joy for me,

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.379
when you come on the
program and it's really,

00:09:04.379 --> 00:09:06.850
I'm also really happy
that you're out there,

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.210
and you're making good music,
and you're doing your thing.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.043
And don't forget this summer. I'm on tour.

00:09:10.043 --> 00:09:10.876
He's on tour and he's also
got an album Ringo Rama,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.293
which is out there Ringo Starr.

00:09:16.293 --> 00:09:17.700
He'll be back at the end of the show.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.250
We'll be right back with Eddie.

